   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Word order with time expressions",
     "texto": [
      "If a time expression comes first, the conjugated verb takes second place: Om morgenen står jeg opp («In the morning I get up»). English usually keeps the subject before the verb, but in Norwegian the verb comes before the subject here.",
      "In a main clause, ofte («often»), alltid («always») and aldri («never») usually come after the conjugated verb: Jeg jobber ofte.",
      "After må («have to») comes the infinitive without å: Jeg må jobbe («I have to work»). Do not add å before the infinitive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
